<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joan, Countess of Toulouse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1220">1220</a>–<a href="/years/1271">1271</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Joan of Toulouse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joan was the only child and heiress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-vii-count-of-toulouse">Raymond VII, Count of Toulouse</a>. Under the Treaty of Paris of 1229, which ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>, she was married to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alphonse-count-of-poitiers">Alphonse of Poitiers</a>, brother of Louis IX. When she and Alphonse died childless within days of each other in 1271, the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> passed to the French crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joan-countess-of-toulouse.jpg" alt="Joan, Countess of Toulouse" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cartes Postales Labouche · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeanne_de_Toulouse.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
